[{"id":2928963316,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ulG70","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?u=febc5a127181f20863d3d34c300625f7ce78ca8f&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","login":"beicause","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107547#pullrequestreview-2928963316","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107547","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-15T04:55:08Z"},{"id":3182942903,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc69t9q3","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"c43090db2ab5c6a6ace96486562c53143da179c2","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nExample with an error in a shader include:\r\n\r\n```\r\n--res://d.gdshader--\r\n    1 | shader_type spatial;\r\n    2 | \r\nE   3-> #include \"res://test.gdshaderinc\"\r\n    4 | \r\n    5 | \r\n--res://test.gdshaderinc--\r\n    7 | \r\n    8 | \r\nE   9-> const int TEST = 225x;\r\n   10 | \r\n   11 | \r\n  ERROR: res://test.gdshaderinc:9 - Invalid (hexadecimal) numeric constant\r\n  ERROR: Shader compilation failed.\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that the shortened errors don't apply to errors in [core shaders](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/core_and_modules/internal_rendering_architecture.html#doc-internal-rendering-architecture-core-shaders), which are still printed in full in all renderers. We could probably change this in a future PR and make them only print 4 lines around the error unless `--verbose` is used.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107547#pullrequestreview-3182942903","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107547","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-09-04T00:17:53Z"},{"id":3183298605,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc69vUgt","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"c43090db2ab5c6a6ace96486562c53143da179c2","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"Makes sense to me! The goal of printing out the shader is to help people identify shader errors for shaders not open in the shader editor. We just need to give them enough information to find where the error is coming from. The entire shader is definitely not needed","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107547#pullrequestreview-3183298605","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107547","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-09-04T03:34:22Z"},{"id":2931013276,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6us7ac","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"c43090db2ab5c6a6ace96486562c53143da179c2","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://av